    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5774bde1_2fea5e8d",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/metrics/NetworkRequestStateStatsMetrics.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 161,
      "author": {
        "id": 1984276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-13T11:22:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, you understood correctly.\n\nThe reason for it is that during some tests I made with my device I saw there can be quite a few network requests, so this is kind of safety measure to make sure we won\u0027t loose any other atoms because of too frequent network requests.",
      "parentUuid": "1ef7149a_ee94e09c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 161,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b26436eeaa4389984068812f7ca6bb1f8699fb05",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7227becb_79366021",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/metrics/NetworkRequestStateStatsMetrics.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 161,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-13T13:23:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not familiar with StatsD code but I think `ConnectivityStatsLog.write` should not lose the atoms even if we call this frequently.\nDid we have this issue before?\n\n@lifr@google.com Do you have any idea? I think our code calls `StatsLog.write` in some places, do we have any rate limiting?",
      "parentUuid": "5774bde1_2fea5e8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 161,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b26436eeaa4389984068812f7ca6bb1f8699fb05",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2c9a801_01027ebc",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/metrics/NetworkRequestStateStatsMetrics.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
